    {
      "path": ".github/workflows/quality.yml",
      "scope": "workflow",
      "job": null,
      "present": true,
      "snippet": "  contents: read\n# `github.ref` is `refs/pull/<N>/merge` for a pull_request event, so this group key is already\n# unique per PR NUMBER and is entirely independent of the PR's BASE branch -- widening the\n# trigger above therefore cannot make two PRs share a group, and needs no change here.\n# Deliberately NOT switched to `github.head_ref || github.ref`: `head_ref` is the SOURCE branch,\n# so two PRs opened from one head (exactly what a stack plus an auto-retarget produces) would\n# collide and cancel each other -- the over-broad-group trap. A manual `workflow_dispatch` on a\n# branch lands in `quality-refs/heads/<branch>`, a different group from that branch's PR run, so\n# the two can run concurrently; that is ACCEPTED rather than merged, because every key that would\n# merge those two also merges runs that must not cancel each other."
    },
